      "file": "src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
      "function": "tokenize",
      "line": 3269,
      "operands": [
        "parseCtx->tokenCount"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "same_object",
        "left": "parseCtx->tokenCount",
        "right": "parseCtx->tokenCount",
        "description": "Source identity relation for the vulnerability-relevant value."
      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 2,
      "description": "jsmn_parse consumes the attacker-controlled JSON input and produces the token array. For the PoC input {\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"}'Type', jsmn produces tokenCount=4 and token[0].size=2 (counting key and value strings as individual children). This structure causes searchObjectForKeyRec to iterate beyond the object's structural boundary and match the stray 'Type' token."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "inv_bounds_check_after_increment",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
      "function": "searchObjectForKeyRec",
      "line": 2267,
      "operands": [
        "parseCtx->index",
        "parseCtx->tokenCount"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "parseCtx->index",
        "right": "parseCtx->tokenCount"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "A_root",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "After finding the key 'Type' at the last valid token (index=3), the code increments parseCtx->index to 4 without checking whether 4 < parseCtx->tokenCount. The out-of-bounds index 4 is then stored in *resultIndex and returned as a valid result. The fix adds a bounds check: if (parseCtx->index >= parseCtx->tokenCount) return UA_STATUSCODE_BADOUTOFRANGE."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "inv_oob_read_at_sink",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
      "function": "Variant_decodeJson",
      "line": 2635,
      "operands": [
        "parseCtx->tokenCount",
        "searchResultType"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "parseCtx->tokenCount",
        "right": "searchResultType"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "A_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 6,
      "description": "Reads parseCtx->tokenArray[searchResultType].type where searchResultType=4 is one past the last valid token (tokenCount=4). The slot contains uninitialized heap data from the UA_malloc allocation. MSAN reports use-of-uninitialized-value at this line."
    },
    {
